% No publications yet.
%
% IMPORTANT: this file is parsed by jekyll-scholar on every build. A BibTeX
% parser latches onto the first "at" sign it sees and tries to read an entry
% from there, even inside what looks like a comment -- so do not leave a
% commented-out template entry in here. It will break the build.
%
% To add a paper, append a normal entry (inproceedings, article, misc, ...).
% Beyond the standard BibTeX fields, al-folio understands these extras:
%
%   selected={true}    also show it in the "selected papers" block on the front
%                      page. Requires selected_papers: true in _pages/about.md,
%                      which is currently false.
%   preview={foo.png}  filename in assets/img/publication_preview/. This renders
%                      the thumbnail beside the entry and is the single highest
%                      value field -- it turns a wall of text into something
%                      scannable.
%   abstract={...}     adds an expandable "Abs" button.
%   arxiv={2601.00000} adds an arXiv link.
%   code={https://...} adds a code link.
%   bibtex_show={true} adds a "Bib" button revealing the BibTeX.
%
% Once there is a real entry here, set nav: true in _pages/publications.md so
% the tab appears in the navbar.
